        "code": {
          "text": "Social and performance situation avoidance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Increasing avoidance over the last 3–4 months: often turns the camera off or joins team video meetings by audio only, avoids monthly in-person office days, and skips social events including birthdays, drinks, and small dinners."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Anxiety in social and performance contexts"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Symptoms present for more than 2 years in most social or performance contexts involving perceived scrutiny. When required to attend, reports anxiety for days beforehand, poor sleep the night before, palpitations, sweating, tremor, nausea, mind going blank, and strong fear of saying something stupid or being judged. Often leaves early or switches the camera off to calm down."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Functional impact of anxiety"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports increased work stress and isolation and turning down promotion opportunities involving presentations."
      }
    },
    {
